	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(780.0, 369.0, 502.0, 487.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">last_review is a Unix timestamp (seconds since 1 Jan 1970), so the (1782172800 - last_review) gives seconds, and divided by 86400 converts to days. 

1782172800 = 23 June 2026, this is the scrape date.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(1075.0, 518.0, 205.0, 69.0)" font-family=".AppleSystemUIFont" font-size="16">Distribution of days since last review across all listings

This is right skewed as most listings have recent reviews, listings that don't have reviews for a while are fewer, this is likely due to the fact that if an AirBnB doesnt have people reviewing for a while than they do not have people staying there and so it is would not be successful for the hosts and likely removed from AirBnB.

There could also be listings that do not have any reviews for several months as they are located in a seasonal destination where they have high and low seasons.</text>
	</annotations>
